state_delta.terraform_infra:
Here is the complete, modular, production-grade Google Cloud Terraform (HCL) implementation adhering to all architectural, networking, and security hardening specifications.

---

### File Structure Overview
```
├── versions.tf        # Provider versions and backend constraints
├── variables.tf       # Input variables with validation and defaults
├── network.tf         # VPC, subnets, PSA peering, Cloud Router, Cloud NAT, and firewall rules
├── security.tf        # Cloud KMS CMEK keys, IAM service accounts, and Cloud Armor WAF policy
├── services.tf        # Google Project APIs, Cloud Storage bucket, Secret Manager, and Cloud SQL HA
├── compute.tf         # Serverless VPC Access Connector and Cloud Run v2 microservices
├── loadbalancer.tf    # Global External HTTPS Load Balancer, SSL policies, and Serverless NEGs
└── outputs.tf         # Key resource identifiers, endpoints, and connectivity attributes
```

---

### 1. `versions.tf`

```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.5.0"

  required_providers {
    google = {
      source  = "hashicorp/google"
      version = "~> 5.0"
    }
    google-beta = {
      source  = "hashicorp/google-beta"
      version = "~> 5.0"
    }
    random = {
      source  = "hashicorp/random"
      version = "~> 3.5"
    }
  }
}

provider "google" {
  project = var.project_id
  region  = var.region
}

provider "google-beta" {
  project = var.project_id
  region  = var.region
}
```

---

### 2. `variables.tf`

```hcl
variable "project_id" {
  description = "The target Google Cloud Project ID where resources will be provisioned."
  type        = string
}

variable "region" {
  description = "The primary GCP region for all regional infrastructure components."
